# HTTP Client

Outbound HTTP subsystem for OpenCart integrations.

This package provides a single, reusable way to call external services from the
project. It is intentionally separate from OpenCart's incoming `Request` and
`Response` runtime classes.

## What It Does

- Uses `cURL` as the transport core
- Keeps request building and transport execution in one place
- Supports JSON, form, multipart, headers, cookies, proxy, auth, and retries
- Normalizes transport and HTTP status failures into exceptions
- Keeps secure defaults enabled by default

## Quick Start

Resolve the client through DI or the helper:

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

use Opencart\System\Library\Http\HttpClient;

$http_client = http_client();
// or: $http_client = app(HttpClient::class);
```

Perform a simple GET request:

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

$response = http_client()->get('https://api.example.com/status');

if ($response->isSuccessful()) {
    $payload = $response->json();
}
```

## Common Examples

### JSON Request

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

$response = http_client()->post('https://api.example.com/orders', [
    'json' => [
        'order_id' => 123,
        'status' => 'paid',
    ],
    'headers' => [
        'Accept' => 'application/json',
    ],
    'timeout' => 15,
]);
```

### Query Parameters

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

$response = http_client()->get('https://api.example.com/search', [
    'query' => [
        'q' => 'catalog',
        'page' => 1,
    ],
]);
```

### Multipart Upload

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

$response = http_client()->post('https://api.example.com/upload', [
    'multipart' => [
        [
            'name' => 'file',
            'path' => '/tmp/report.csv',
            'mime' => 'text/csv',
            'filename' => 'report.csv',
        ],
        [
            'name' => 'source',
            'contents' => 'admin-panel',
        ],
    ],
]);
```

### Retry Policy

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

$response = http_client()->get('https://api.example.com/health', [
    'retry_attempts' => 3,
    'retry_delay_milliseconds' => 250,
    'retry_status_codes' => [429, 500, 502, 503, 504],
]);
```

### Handling Failures

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

use Opencart\System\Library\Http\Exception\HttpResponseException;
use Opencart\System\Library\Http\Exception\HttpTransportException;

try {
    $response = http_client()->get('https://api.example.com/profile');
} catch (HttpTransportException $exception) {
    // Network or cURL failure.
} catch (HttpResponseException $exception) {
    // Non-success HTTP status when throw_on_http_error is enabled.
}
```

## Security Defaults

- TLS verification is enabled by default
- Redirects are limited and restricted to HTTP/HTTPS
- Headers and payloads are not logged by default
- Caller-provided overrides must be explicit

## Files

- `client.php` - main HTTP client
- `request/http_request.php` - outbound request DTO
- `response/http_response.php` - outbound response DTO
- `transport/curl_transport.php` - cURL adapter
- `exception/*.php` - transport and response exceptions
- `helper/http.php` - `httpClient()` helper

## Integration Notes

- Register new transports behind `HttpTransportInterface`
- Keep outbound HTTP code separate from incoming OpenCart request/response flow
- Prefer this client over ad hoc `curl_*` usage in new code

## See Also

- [AI Factory Architecture](../../../../.ai-factory/ARCHITECTURE.md) - project-level rules for the HTTP layer
- [Project Guidelines](../../../../AGENTS.md) - repository conventions and documentation map
